  <section id="made" class="prose">
    <h2>Made in the studio shown here</h2>
    <p>We used the studio we built to produce the App Composer artwork and motion used on this page.</p>
    <p>That sentence is a chain, not a caption. The project is <strong>App Composer — studio launch artwork</strong>, kept in the same deployed studio as the earlier work. The brief asked for an editorial illustration about owning a studio: tactile paper, warm ink, a controlled orange signal route and room for exact type. The first still came from Workers AI Lucid Origin at 1280×720. The selected refinement was a real masked fill: a white ellipse in the empty upper-right panel, a prompt for a paper signal ring, and FLUX.1 Fill returning a 1280×704 variant while the original, the mask and the result stayed separate. The motion is Hailuo 2.3 animating that selected edit; the sound bed is a separate Studio Effect. The type, mark, crops and the 9:16 frame were then finished deterministically, because generated lettering and a generated logo would be the wrong tool.</p>
